## Purpose

Keep the technical CI green while the emblem is honestly still under visual review.

## Change

- `not-reference-approved` no longer throws by itself;
- all integrity, provenance, blob-lock, score-range and artifact checks remain blocking;
- a false `reference-accepted` decision still fails unless the acceptance floor and every per-category threshold are met and blocking deviations are empty;
- GitHub Actions now shows a changing progress notice and step summary, for example `61% — developing candidate`;
- green CI is explicitly described as technical integrity only, not proof of visual fidelity.

## Conflict safety

This PR contains one validator file only and targets the bot's working branch rather than `main`, so it does not modify the emblem geometry or interrupt the ongoing visual pass.

