## Exact base

- `main@90dfaade9b9fb13ecb27712b95ad334455e9db59`
- head `1996fc196a9ef98b14dc7e48856439f88256c15c`
- three diagnostic-only files; no production source changes.

## Why this exists

Merged PR #162 has green CI and a green desktop/Pixel/iPhone browser matrix, and its normal iPhone first-viewport screenshot is correct. However, the retained reduced-motion iPhone screenshot is visually blank even though its JSON reports final opacity, transform and animation values.

## Evidence sequence

The production build is captured on iPhone 15 Pro WebKit with `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` at seven stages:

1. immediately after all six portraits decode;
2. after two animation frames;
3. after 250 ms;
4. after 1000 ms;
5. direct hero element screenshot;
6. after cancelling subtree animations and setting final inline state;
7. after a display/reflow repaint.

Each stage stores full viewport screenshots plus computed style, bounds, media state, animation timing and hit-test JSON. This will distinguish screenshot timing from a retained WebKit compositing layer.

Close without merge after artifact inspection; implement any real fix in a separate clean PR from current main.

