## Confirmed visual bug

The final exact-head screenshots for brand v4 showed that mobile premium windows still rendered:

- `Михаил Лермон…`;
- `Александр Пуш…`;
- `Владимир Маяко…`.

The cause was the Tailwind `truncate` utility on the name element, which forces `white-space: nowrap`, hidden overflow and ellipsis even though touch labels are permanently visible.

## Fix

- remove the forced single-line truncation;
- add a stable `data-hero-poet-window-name` hook;
- balance each full name across one or two centered lines;
- keep panel height stable with a two-line minimum;
- preserve normal word boundaries, disable hyphenation and use compact mobile tracking/padding;
- leave portraits, 3D pointer pipeline, brand v4 and deploy contracts untouched.

## Permanent regression contract

A new focused test runs in desktop Chromium, Pixel 7 Chromium and iPhone 15 Pro WebKit and requires:

- exact order and exact complete text of all six names;
- no `text-overflow: ellipsis`;
- no `white-space: nowrap`;
- no horizontal or vertical text clipping;
- one or two balanced lines only;
- decoded portraits and zero page errors;
- fresh first-viewport screenshots and JSON geometry facts.

## Scope

- `.github/workflows/manual-browser-qa.yml`
- `playwright.home-polish.config.mjs`
- `qa/home-labels.spec.mjs`
- `src/components/home/HeroPoetWindow.tsx`
- `src/components/home/hero-poet-window.css`

Keep unmerged until exact CI, broad Chromium/Pixel/iPhone QA and the expanded home matrix pass on the current v4 main baseline.

