## Superseded by a newer main baseline — closed without merge

This PR correctly produced and tested a two-parent sync for canonical `d312dd9f…` and the then-current `main@68f7a615…`. It must not merge because `main` advanced during its exact-head QA.

The new `main@1cf00ce72adbe6c52abdecb4b7e633bfda9df815` is a materially different brand contract, not an additive follow-up:

- replaces the prior hooded-book SVG with the owner-selected faceless hooded figure master;
- removes book, wings and halo from the canonical emblem;
- introduces deterministic `brand:materialize` from committed base64 source parts;
- changes platform raster storage/materialization;
- changes `BrandMark`, favicon/mask, OG image from PNG to JPEG, metadata and prerender defaults;
- rewrites brand QA and static validation accordingly.

Therefore the old five-file sync tree would reintroduce superseded brand assumptions and cannot be accepted even if its CI/Browser runs finish green.

Frozen facts from this PR:

- exact head `b00383626eb4f1323b55cbe2d191fbffd30dbbb1`;
- canonical first parent `d312dd9f269955f564cad3e80c3d0d43e4c56b33`;
- obsolete main second parent `68f7a6151e6371349724e3549d85e612980ca020`;
- no canonical or main branch mutation occurred;
- close without merge.

A new conflict-aware sync must be built from the then-current canonical head and the final settled main head after the active home-polish contour is resolved. It must preserve research CI/package/prerender validators while adopting the new selected-emblem materialization contract.

